# Stage 08a — Per-chapter post-translation control (GATE)

Follow `skills/expert-translation-quality/SKILL.md` and
`skills/translation-quality-defect-families/SKILL.md`.

For EACH authorized translated chapter, run a FULL-CHAPTER (not sampled) post-translation
control. Read the committed `chapters/translated/{NNN_slug}.md`, write the corrected immutable
revision to `chapters/controlled/{NNN_slug}.md`, and write
`qa/chapter_controls/{NNN_slug}.control.md`. Never overwrite or adopt the committed translated
artifact. The check must cover
body text, notes, terminology, reader-facing wording, readability, polish,
plain-language clarity (without flattening specialist quality), title handling,
and text interfaces for any figures/tables/formulas/images.

Include a Chinese-only readability pass (read the translation without the source
first). Fix any issue found in the new controlled revision, then append a fresh
recheck round. A round where issues were fixed is `FIXED_RECHECK_REQUIRED`, not PASS.

Each control file's latest round must end with these machine-readable fields:
```
scope: FULL_CHAPTER
issues_found: 0
fixes_applied: 0
unresolved_blocking_issues: 0
latest_round_status: PASS
allow_next_chapter: true
expert_translation_skill_used: true
polysemy_unresolved_count: 0
```

Exit condition: every authorized chapter has a zero-issue PASS control file.
Stop for controller validation; do not modify gate or control state.
